      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "salesforce-case-baseline-hydration-and-reconciliation",
      "documentConcept": "Salesforce Case baseline hydration and reconciliation",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:7b9fcad757689235d71ba3356854fc7dde446afcb966378f7c1c608c697a7c98",
      "text": "A Case alert projection needs an initial population and a way to repair drift. The design here combines baseline SOQL reads with ongoing change consumption. Baseline reads must follow pagination. Salesforce documents API rereads for record-level gaps, full entity synchronization for overflow, explicit deletion reconciliation, and replay to catch changes made during synchronization. Its polling replication cursor also accounts for unfinished transactions. These are projection-repair mechanisms; the sources do not establish one atomic snapshot-to-stream handoff algorithm for this application.",
